@page "/admin/architecture"

<PageTitle>Hotel architecture</PageTitle>

<section class="architecture-page" aria-labelledby="architecture-title">
    <AdminNav />
    <header class="architecture-heading">
        <p class="eyebrow">Repository-sourced service map</p>
        <h1 id="architecture-title">Hotel services and delivery path</h1>
        <p>
            This explains configured repository paths and declared resource tiers. It is not a live
            service-health or delivery-status view, and does not prove a cloud connection is active.
        </p>
        <div class="diagram-legend" aria-label="Diagram legend">
            <span><i class="legend-line" aria-hidden="true"></i> Configured or declared relationship</span>
            <span><i class="legend-dot" aria-hidden="true"></i> Decorative moving dot; not live traffic</span>
            <span>Every connector is numbered and labelled with its configured call or delivery action; matching explanations follow below.</span>
        </div>
    </header>

    <section class="architecture-section" aria-labelledby="service-map-title">
        <p class="eyebrow">Hotel services only</p>
        <h2 id="service-map-title">Service map</h2>
        <p class="section-intro">
            The numbered, labelled lines illustrate repository-declared calls and delivery
            responsibilities. They are a static diagram: no live traffic or telemetry is queried.
        </p>

        <div class="service-paths">
            <section aria-labelledby="booking-path-title">
                <h3 id="booking-path-title">Guest booking and operations</h3>
                <ol class="service-flow" aria-label="Guest booking service path">
                    <li>
                        <article class="service-card">
                            <span class="service-number">1</span>
                            <h4>Static Web Apps</h4>
                            <p>Hosts the Blazor WebAssembly booking UI.</p>
                        </article>
                        <span class="service-connector"><span class="connector-label">1 · HTTPS/API</span></span>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <article class="service-card">
                            <span class="service-number">2</span>
                            <h4>App Service</h4>
                            <p>ASP.NET Core booking API and its hosted SignalR operations hub.</p>
                        </article>
                        <span class="service-connector"><span class="connector-label">2 · Managed identity / EF Core</span></span>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <article class="service-card">
                            <span class="service-number">3</span>
                            <h4>Azure SQL</h4>
                            <p>Hotel catalog, rooms, reservations, and bounded operations events.</p>
                        </article>
                    </li>
                </ol>
            </section>

            <section aria-labelledby="telemetry-path-title">
                <h3 id="telemetry-path-title">API telemetry destination</h3>
                <ol class="service-flow" aria-label="API telemetry configuration path">
                    <li>
                        <article class="service-card">
                            <span class="service-number">1</span>
                            <h4>App Service API</h4>
                            <p>Application Insights connection is configured for the API.</p>
                        </article>
                        <span class="service-connector"><span class="connector-label">1 · Telemetry configuration</span></span>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <article class="service-card">
                            <span class="service-number">2</span>
                            <h4>Application Insights</h4>
                            <p>Receives configured API telemetry.</p>
                        </article>
                        <span class="service-connector"><span class="connector-label">2 · Workspace-backed</span></span>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <article class="service-card">
                            <span class="service-number">3</span>
                            <h4>Log Analytics workspace</h4>
                            <p>Backs Application Insights and retains logs.</p>
                        </article>
                    </li>
                </ol>
                <p class="flow-note">Configuration does not prove live telemetry is being emitted.</p>
            </section>

            <section aria-labelledby="routing-path-title">
                <h3 id="routing-path-title">Runtime routing services</h3>
                <ol class="service-flow" aria-label="Runtime routing service path">
                    <li>
                        <article class="service-card">
                            <span class="service-number">1</span>
                            <h4>App Service API</h4>
                            <p>Deterministic C# policy owns safety and evidence gates.</p>
                        </article>
                        <span class="service-connector"><span class="connector-label">1 · Prompt Shields check</span></span>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <article class="service-card">
                            <span class="service-number">2</span>
                            <h4>Azure AI Content Safety</h4>
                            <p>Prompt Shields checks routing metadata before an optional suggestion.</p>
                        </article>
                        <span class="service-connector"><span class="connector-label">2 · API search after safety</span></span>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <article class="service-card">
                            <span class="service-number">3</span>
                            <h4>Azure AI Search</h4>
                            <p>Checks evidence against the exact requested knowledge revision.</p>
                        </article>
                        <span class="service-connector"><span class="connector-label">3 · Conditional model call</span></span>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <article class="service-card">
                            <span class="service-number">4</span>
                            <h4>Azure OpenAI via Microsoft Agent Framework</h4>
                            <p>Optional bounded choice only when multiple safe workers remain.</p>
                        </article>
                    </li>
                </ol>
                <p class="flow-note">
                    Safety, grounding, and model failure route to human review. The model cannot grant
                    permissions or approve delivery; the API returns a routing decision.
                </p>
            </section>

            <section aria-labelledby="delivery-path-title">
                <h3 id="delivery-path-title">Requirement-to-deployment path</h3>
                <ol class="service-flow delivery-service-flow" aria-label="Azure Boards and GitHub delivery path" tabindex="0">
                    <li>
                        <article class="service-card">
                            <span class="service-number">1</span>
                            <h4>Azure Boards</h4>
                            <p>Requirement, acceptance criteria, and work-item state.</p>
                        </article>
                        <span class="service-connector"><span class="connector-label">1 · Scheduled query</span></span>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <article class="service-card">
                            <span class="service-number">2</span>
                            <h4>GitHub Actions intake</h4>
                            <p>Queries Boards and creates or reuses the linked GitHub issue.</p>
                        </article>
                        <span class="service-connector"><span class="connector-label">2 · Linked issue + assignment</span></span>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <article class="service-card">
                            <span class="service-number">3</span>
                            <h4>GitHub issue + cloud agent</h4>
                            <p>The assigned agent implements the bounded requirement.</p>
                        </article>
                        <span class="service-connector"><span class="connector-label">3 · Agent opens PR</span></span>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <article class="service-card">
                            <span class="service-number">4</span>
                            <h4>Pull request + evidence gates</h4>
                            <p>Validation, Copilot review, and QA verify the proposed revision.</p>
                        </article>
                        <span class="service-connector"><span class="connector-label">4 · Evidence-passed merge</span></span>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <article class="service-card">
                            <span class="service-number">5</span>
                            <h4>Development deployment</h4>
                            <p>Actions deploys the merged revision to the development environment.</p>
                        </article>
                    </li>
                </ol>
            </section>
        </div>
    </section>

    <section class="architecture-section" aria-labelledby="flow-explanations-title">
        <h2 id="flow-explanations-title">Numbered flow explanations</h2>
        <ol class="flow-explanations">
            <li><strong>Booking 1–2:</strong> Static Web Apps serves Blazor files; the UI calls the App Service API over HTTPS. The API uses managed identity and EF Core to access SQL.</li>
            <li><strong>Telemetry 1–2:</strong> the API is configured to send telemetry to Application Insights; the Log Analytics workspace backs the component. This configuration is not proof of live telemetry.</li>
            <li><strong>Routing 1–3:</strong> the API calls Prompt Shields, then performs exact-revision Search after safety passes; Microsoft Agent Framework may make a conditional Azure OpenAI call only when multiple safe workers remain.</li>
            <li><strong>Delivery 1–4:</strong> Boards is queried by scheduled intake; Actions links an issue and assigns the cloud agent; the agent opens a PR; evidence-gated merge precedes development deployment.</li>
        </ol>
    </section>

    <section class="architecture-section" aria-labelledby="sku-title">
        <h2 id="sku-title">Declared tier and responsibility</h2>
        <p class="flow-note">
            Tiers below are sourced from Bicep, not live resource discovery or pricing. SaaS products
            without a repository-declared Azure SKU are identified as such.
        </p>
        <div class="sku-card-grid" role="list" aria-label="Repository-declared service tiers and responsibilities">
            <article class="sku-card" role="listitem">
                <h3>Static Web Apps</h3>
                <dl><dt>Declared tier / SKU</dt><dd>Free</dd><dt>Responsibility</dt><dd>Blazor WebAssembly files and client-side routing.</dd><dt>Source</dt><dd><code>infra/modules/platform.bicep</code></dd></dl>
            </article>
            <article class="sku-card" role="listitem">
                <h3>App Service plan</h3>
                <dl><dt>Declared tier / SKU</dt><dd>Basic B1</dd><dt>Responsibility</dt><dd>ASP.NET Core API and API-hosted SignalR hub.</dd><dt>Source</dt><dd><code>infra/modules/platform.bicep</code></dd></dl>
            </article>
            <article class="sku-card" role="listitem">
                <h3>Azure SQL Database</h3>
                <dl><dt>Declared tier / SKU</dt><dd>GP_S_Gen5 serverless GeneralPurpose, capacity 1; minCapacity 0.5 vCore, auto-pause 60 min</dd><dt>Responsibility</dt><dd>Catalog, reservations, and bounded event persistence.</dd><dt>Source</dt><dd><code>infra/modules/platform.bicep</code></dd></dl>
            </article>
            <article class="sku-card" role="listitem">
                <h3>Azure AI Search</h3>
                <dl><dt>Declared tier / SKU</dt><dd>Basic; 1 replica, 1 partition; semantic search Free</dd><dt>Responsibility</dt><dd>Revisioned knowledge evidence lookup.</dd><dt>Source</dt><dd><code>infra/modules/platform.bicep</code></dd></dl>
            </article>
            <article class="sku-card" role="listitem">
                <h3>Azure AI Services</h3>
                <dl><dt>Declared tier / SKU</dt><dd>S0; Azure OpenAI deployment gpt-4.1-mini GlobalStandard, capacity 10</dd><dt>Responsibility</dt><dd>Content Safety Prompt Shields and optional model suggestion via Microsoft Agent Framework.</dd><dt>Source</dt><dd><code>infra/modules/platform.bicep</code></dd></dl>
            </article>
            <article class="sku-card" role="listitem">
                <h3>Application Insights + Log Analytics</h3>
                <dl><dt>Declared tier / SKU</dt><dd>Workspace-backed; 30-day workspace retention</dd><dt>Responsibility</dt><dd>API telemetry and log retention.</dd><dt>Source</dt><dd><code>infra/modules/platform.bicep</code></dd></dl>
            </article>
            <article class="sku-card" role="listitem">
                <h3>Azure Boards + GitHub Actions</h3>
                <dl><dt>Declared tier / SKU</dt><dd>Hosted SaaS; no Azure resource SKU declared here</dd><dt>Responsibility</dt><dd>Boards manages work state; Actions performs intake, verification, and deployment.</dd><dt>Source</dt><dd><code>.github/workflows/</code> and <code>docs/knowledge/agentic-delivery.md</code></dd></dl>
            </article>
        </div>
    </section>

    <section class="architecture-section" aria-labelledby="end-to-end-title">
        <h2 id="end-to-end-title">End-to-end delivery flow</h2>
        <p class="section-intro">Development and production are separate. A release proposal never deploys production; promotion is a distinct human-approved manual path.</p>
        <ol class="end-to-end-flow" tabindex="0" aria-label="End-to-end delivery stages, horizontally scrollable">
            <li>Boards intake</li><li>GitHub issue + cloud agent</li><li>Pull request</li>
            <li>PR validation</li><li>Copilot review gate</li><li>QA evidence</li>
            <li>Merge</li><li>Development deployment</li><li>Lifecycle sync + evidence</li>
            <li>Release proposal</li><li>Human production approval</li>
        </ol>
        <p class="proposal-note">
            <strong>Coordinator proposal, not implemented:</strong> durable stage coordination with
            per-stage evidence envelopes and deterministic readiness policy. Microsoft-Decision-1
            recovery classification is proposed for shadow mode only and must not influence retries,
            permissions, gate outcomes, merges, or release approval.
            <a href="https://github.com/cihanduruer/agentic-development/blob/main/docs/knowledge/agentic-delivery.md"
               target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Read the proposal and its limits</a>.
        </p>
    </section>
</section>
